    <string name="dialog_decay_formula_desc" formatted="false">• Daily Decay = (Initial Health - Latest Health) ÷ Sampling Days\n• Monthly Decay = Daily Decay × 30.44 days; Yearly Est = Daily Decay × 365.25 days\n• Daily Cycle Consumption = Total Cycle Increase ÷ Sampling Days\n• Monthly Cycle = Daily Cycle × 30.44 days; Yearly Est = Daily Cycle × 365.25 days\n• Lithium batteries typically decay to ~80% after 300~500 cycles (~4%~8% yearly decay, ~0.5~1.2 cycles/day is normal).</string>
